winemac: HORZRES and VERTRES are not doubled in retina mode.

From athei/wine fa43d6db2 ("winemac: Don't double HORZRES and VERTRES in retina mode",
LGPL like Wine). macdrv_GetDeviceCaps doubled both caps whenever retina mode was on, on top of
the fallback that already reports monitors in pixels, so a retina process saw the screen twice as
large there as through GetSystemMetrics and EnumDisplaySettings.

Measured on an M4 (1920x1080 display, macOS 27.0, 2026-10-06) with a probe on x64-crossover26.3-r17,
the same on the default Wine 10 engine: Retina resolution off, every call says 1920x1080. Retina on,
GetSystemMetrics, EnumDisplaySettings and DESKTOPHORZRES say 3840x2160 and HORZRES/VERTRES say
7680x4320. Team Fortress 2 centres its window from HORZRES (athei), and Red Dead Redemption 2 at
1920x1080 fullscreen comes out cropped for a player with Retina on (highball#261).

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -213,15 +213,10 @@ static INT macdrv_GetDeviceCaps(PHYSDEV dev, INT cap)
     case VERTSIZE:
         ret = vert_size;
         break;
-    case HORZRES:
-    case VERTRES:
     default:
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
         dev = GET_NEXT_PHYSDEV( dev, pGetDeviceCaps );
-        ret = dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
-        if ((cap == HORZRES || cap == VERTRES) && retina_on)
-            ret *= 2;
-        return ret;
+        return dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
     }
 
     TRACE("cap %d -> %d\n", cap, ret);
